<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The app's own face, for the launcher to draw with.

    Every word inside this app is set in itfQomra — see AppTheme._fontFamily —
    and a widget in the launcher's default font is the one difference a reader
    notices before any other, because it is the one that makes the pane look
    like it belongs to somebody else's app. Flutter's copy of this font lives in
    assets/ and is loaded by the engine; nothing here is running an engine, so
    the two weights the widget uses are carried again as Android resources.

    Only 400 and 700. The Light face is never asked for on the widget's face,
    and a third weight is 55KB for nothing.

    Honoured from API 26. On 24 and 25 the framework reads android:fontFamily as
    a family NAME rather than a resource, fails to match, and falls back to the
    system font — the widget is then plain but perfectly legible, which is the
    right way for this to degrade.
-->
<font-family xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <font
        android:font="@font/itf_qomra_regular"
        android:fontStyle="normal"
        android:fontWeight="400" />
    <font
        android:font="@font/itf_qomra_bold"
        android:fontStyle="normal"
        android:fontWeight="700" />
</font-family>
